    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="d14-1" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d14-1"/>

                <head>15. Telegram 249 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d15-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-08-02">August 2, 1955, 8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d15-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d15-1"/>
                <p>249. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>This morning CHICOM Ambassador Berlin told same source mentioned Mytel 226 that
                    American civilians under arrest in China <pb facs="0065" n="18" type="typeset"
                        xml:id="pg18"/> now being collected near Peiping in anticipation early
                    repatriation; that CHICOMS are going propose bilateral agreement with US to
                    renounce use force settlement any “international” questions; CHICOMS willing
                    agree not use force against Formosa if can obtain possession Matsu and Quemoy
                    and US recognizes CHICOM “peaceful claim” to Formosa; CHICOMS will not agree any
                    internationalization Fomosa; and Wang is going press me for early FonMin
                    conference preferably September at which all outstanding issues would be
                    discussed. Also last week CHICOMS delivered strong note to Soviets expressing
                    “disapproval” of failure Soviets press Far Eastern matters harder at
                    conference.</p>
                <p>CHICOMS very “irked” with Soviets at this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
